WEBVTT

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.980
Welcome back, I'm certainly glad you could...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.420
to join me for this, the last show

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.500
of the 10th Joy of Paintings series.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.640
So I tell you what, let's start off

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.300
and have them graphically run all the colors

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.900
across the screen that you need to paint along with me.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.820
While they're doing that, let's go on up here.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.940
We have our standard old 18 by 24 inch canvas.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.320
It's covered with a nice thin even coat of liquid white.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.900
It's all slick and wet and it's ready to go,

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:50.640
so let's start.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.440
I'm gonna start out today with some phthalo blue

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.900
on the brush, just tap the brush right into the blue.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:00:59.980
Just tap it in.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:00.960
like so.

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:02.230
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.870
Let's build us a happy little sky.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:08.020
Let me just take this blue and we'll make some

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.730
little criss cross strokes, like so.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.530
Maybe we'll leave some areas open.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:14.920
We'll have some fun.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.120
We'll play a little bit, just leave them open.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.350
To that blue, I'm gonna add the least little touch

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:21.640
of midnight black.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:24.060
Just wanna, there, yeah.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.130
Make it a little darker in places.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.250
There we go, blue.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:35.080
A little touch of black, there we are.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.680
Now the color is automatically blending

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.750
with liquid white and it gets lighter and lighter

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.350
and lighter down here toward the horizon.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.610
And that's exactly what we're looking for.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.050
Now then, while we have that on the brush,

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:54.240
good ol' blue on the brush, let's come right down here

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.120
and let's put, maybe there'll be a little water down here.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.480
Let's start right down here.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:01.500
Okay, come across this way.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.440
We'll have a little water down the bottom of this painting.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.040
What the devil?

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.040
We can do that if we want.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:11.860
Something about like so.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:16.200
Okay, let me wash the brush.

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:19.390
And we wash our brushes with odorless paint thinner,

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:26.480
shake off the excess, beat the devil out of it.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:29.320
All right, now with a clean brush we go back in here.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:33.020
and very gently just blend.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.880
Just blend, just like so.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.130
See those areas we left now are nice little light areas.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:43.190
We could stop right there and have nice cloud-looking

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:44.130
effects in the sky.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:46.350
Maybe we'll make a happy little cloud today.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:52.690
There, here we just blended the paint out.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.840
And very lightly we'll go across it

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:57.940
to take out the brush strokes.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:02:59.980
And down here, same thing, all the way.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.550
across that little light area that we left.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.220
It remains right there.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.890
It looks like a little sheen of light

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.270
that's going to be playing across the water

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:09.790
when we're done.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:16.880
Okay, and then we can wash your brush again.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.140
That's the fun part of this.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.230
Take out all your frustrations and hostilities,

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:24.580
just like that.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.820
Okay, happy little clouds.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:29.940
We'll grab a one-

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.360
brush, and let's go right into titanium white.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.450
Just pull that brush right through there.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:38.900
We can even go down here and get the least little touch

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:42.320
of the bright red, least, least little touch.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:44.840
Don't get crazy with it, it's very strong.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.270
A lot of pain in the brush.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:48.000
Okay, let's go up here.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:51.150
Now, if we're gonna have a cloud that lives right there,

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:55.180
let's just go right in here using little circles.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:58.050
You could do this with a fan brush or the two-inch brush,

00:03:58.150 --> 00:03:59.980
whatever, I just happen to...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.600
pick up this one, and let's just lay in

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.570
all kinds of beautiful little clouds.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.220
Just sort of let your imagination go crazy.

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.910
Just think like a cloud, just float around the sky,

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:22.090
a good time, so when you're doing this,

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:25.180
just sort of relax and be calm and peaceful,

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.120
enjoy life.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:34.920
Just really, really should bring you a lot of,

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.910
a lot of good feelings here.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.070
Should make you happy.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.940
Painting should really make you happy.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:43.460
If it doesn't make you happy,

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:44.740
then you're doing the wrong thing.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:48.180
There you go.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:50.740
Let's just put another layer here.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.250
Just make a decision.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:53.910
How many clouds you want, drop them in.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:54.740
No big deal.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:56.120
Might even put one up here.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.220
That'll give you a lot of practice.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.720
If there's a secret to this, it's practice.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:04.790
Just practice.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:07.400
Anything that you want to be good at, you practice.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:08.600
And it's the same with painting.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:11.130
The more you practice, the easier it gets.

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:14.620
The more fun you have with it, pretty soon,

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.480
you don't even have to think about

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:17.960
how you're loading the brushes or,

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:20.540
oh, because you know what's gonna happen.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.500
All you have to think about is composition and effects.

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:26.580
That's when it really becomes fun.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:29.970
When you no longer, you no longer have to spend all.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.380
all your thinking time, thinking about,

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.520
now how do I load this brush, or how do I load the knife?

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.090
That will become automatic.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:39.740
Here I'm just blending, take out the little brush strokes,

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.220
corner the brush, just sort of wind this up,

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:49.080
mix it up, just mix, don't overdo, don't overdo.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:52.320
If you blend too much, they'll just disappear.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.120
They'll go away and leave you.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:56.940
You'll be sitting there all by yourself.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.960
But if that happens, you can go right back

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.830
and drop them right back in, it's no problem at all.

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:07.110
Lift up, this just sort of fluffs them,

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.650
makes those nice little fluffy edges.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.780
Just fluffs them up, look at that.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.300
Isn't that a super nice easy way

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.860
to make some fantastic little clouds.

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:22.290
And I beat the brush just to knock

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:23.610
the excess paint off of it.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:26.000
Because I'm lazy and it's easier

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.540
than cleaning the brush all over again.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:29.820
There we go.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:31.620
Isn't that a beautiful little sky?

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:34.000
That quick.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.460
I knew you could do it.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.300
There we are.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.020
Now we can wash your brush.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:43.220
Just shake it off.

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:50.010
Okay, we're in business.

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:51.320
Now, let's see.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.450
Today let's use the old round brush.

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:56.610
I'm gonna go right into some Van Dyke Brown,

00:06:57.010 --> 00:06:57.970
some Dark Sienna.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:06:59.980
Shoo, we'll grab a...

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:03.290
of this Prussian blue, just a touch,

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:05.610
because it's very strong.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:08.510
So we've got both browns and a little Prussian blue,

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:08.970
there it is.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.080
Now then, have to make some decisions.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:15.250
Maybe we'll have a, yep, let's have a little,

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:18.030
a happy little tree that lives right here on the corner.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:20.620
I wanna do maybe, maybe we'll do a little,

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:22.500
a little country scene today.

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:27.660
Have a lot of little trees back here.

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:29.980
This round brush is super, super,

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.380
for doing little background trees, see?

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:35.910
But I start at the bottom and work upward,

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:38.530
that way it gets lighter and lighter and lighter

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:39.450
as it goes up.

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:44.740
So the dark area down here is where all the shadows are.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:50.020
And here not as much light will get through,

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:51.120
so you want that darker.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:53.700
So by starting there and working up your brushes,

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.020
your brush is just running out of paint, that's all.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:59.980
Just make a decision, look at that tree.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.840
That tree just grew on me, just grows and grows.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:09.040
And just however many trees you want in your world.

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:10.580
That's how many there should be.

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:13.830
That's how many there should be.

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:15.880
Maybe right here.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:19.040
You knew that, or didn't you?

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:25.290
Well, we got Tree City right here in a matter of minutes.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.260
We could literally just about fill all this in with color.

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:43.360
I'm tapping quite firmly, you can probably hear that.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:46.120
It's really tapping quite firm.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:48.340
In here, we said there was gonna be some water,

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:49.160
but don't worry about it.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:50.260
Anything that comes down in here,

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:52.140
shoot, we just turn it into reflections.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:57.660
Worry about it, no big deal at all.

00:08:58.040 --> 00:08:59.970
We can fix any.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:00.860
the old thing that happens.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.090
In some of the instructional videotapes we make,

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:08.010
we show how to correct as well as how to make these things,

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:10.930
and that's, to be able to correct is probably

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.630
as important as being able to paint.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:17.190
So we devote a lot of energy to showing you how to do that.

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:22.560
Right, now then, take the liner brush,

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:23.700
little paint thinner on it,

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:26.620
and I wanna thin this paint until it's like water.

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:29.970
Turn that brush and pull it out to a nice sharp point.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:31.810
Look at there, see how sharp it is?

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:32.940
Good, let's go up here.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:36.220
Now here and there, we're gonna put in

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:40.400
the indication of a little tree trunk.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:42.400
Wherever, wherever there is one.

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:45.320
And maybe there's some out here.

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:49.540
No, no worry, just there.

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:54.120
Just relax, enjoy.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:56.460
Just sort of let this happen.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.380
Think like a tree.

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:06.190
There we go, a little more thinner.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:10.590
Any time your paint won't just slide right off the brush,

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:11.690
add some more thinner.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.190
Thin paint will stick to a thick paint.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:16.210
Thin to thick.

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:21.580
Okay, that gives us an indication

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:23.830
of a lot of happy little trees out there.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:26.880
Tell you what, let's take,

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:28.800
I'm gonna go right into...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.060
Use the same old dirty brush.

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:33.560
I'll go right into some midnight black and then some yellow.

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:38.670
Tap that brush, tap it, load a lot of paint.

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:40.450
Same old dirty brush, I'm using the color

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.030
that's already in the brush to mix with this.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:43.860
There was a little bit of blue in that

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.060
so that helps it turn green.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:50.300
There, okay, now right up here, let's start here.

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:53.560
Just touch, all those little sparklers

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:59.640
just jump right off the brush, just there.

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:03.550
Work in layers, work in layers.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:11.500
The brush just does some fantastic things.

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.260
See, make individual trees back here.

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:18.250
We can dip into a little yellow ochre,

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:21.950
then yellow, and then here and there

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:25.220
I'm gonna jump on the bright red bush.

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:28.990
Boy, he's a pretty little devil, he lives right there.

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:33.380
There we go, maybe out here.

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:39.340
There's another one, there's a little piece over here.

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:42.960
See, think about the limbs projecting out and causing,

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:44.970
see there's little clumps here.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:46.870
There's just not a solid green mess.

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:48.030
They're not just hit at random.

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:50.050
See, look at the shapes.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:52.720
Pay particular attention to the shapes.

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:57.270
When you're doing these, don't just hit at random.

00:11:58.710 --> 00:11:59.670
Think about what you're doing.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.020
Look at the trees in your yard.

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:04.190
Take a trip to the woods.

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:09.180
Go out and talk to a tree, make friends with it.

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:12.610
Look at all the little layers and stuff.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:26.280
Just all kinds of little things happening.

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:29.970
We'll put another one.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:31.040
Right in there.

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:33.230
That one's got a little more red in it.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:34.570
It just really jumps out at you.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:36.420
Pretty little rascal.

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:39.080
Pretty little rascal.

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:40.780
Just layer after layer after layer.

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:46.130
I'm just wandering all over here,

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:48.920
dropping all kinds in.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:52.800
Maybe there's one right here.

00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:57.240
If I'm not careful, I'm gonna cover up

00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:58.920
everything I said was gonna be water.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.400
I get carried away, these little rascals are so much fun to make

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:06.020
and they're so pretty, sometimes I just get carried away

00:13:06.020 --> 00:13:07.020
