00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:08.320
Okay, let's come right in here.

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.720
This is gonna be water, let's grab this

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.280
and turn it into reflections.

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:14.650
Pull it straight down, straight down, straight down,

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:21.140
like that, there, that fantastic, now go across.

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:25.490
And that easy, you have instant, instant reflections.

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:27.090
It's very, very simple.

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:29.370
We'll just use that same old brush,

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:29.890
I'm going right in.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.100
to some of the browns again.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:35.690
Let's just lay in a little bit of color here.

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:39.150
We can begin creating all kinds of happy little things.

00:13:41.890 --> 00:13:43.050
These are just the browns.

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:46.020
Least little touch of Prussian blue, but not much.

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:48.550
Mostly browns.

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:53.100
There's a thing that's going on here.

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:05.620
See, we'll just throw this on like that.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:06.440
It doesn't make any difference.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:08.120
All we're looking for right here is just color.

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:12.720
Just applying color to the canvas.

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:17.660
